---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { product } from "../data/product";
import { company } from "../data/company";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`Terms of Service for ${product.name} — version ${product.legalDocsVersion.terms}.`}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-20">
    <header>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-700 uppercase tracking-wide">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
        {product.name} · Version {product.legalDocsVersion.terms} · Last updated:{" "}
        {product.legalDocsVersion.lastUpdated}
      </p>
      <div class="mt-5 rounded-lg border border-indigo-200 bg-indigo-50/40 p-4 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-slate-900">Summary.</strong>
        {product.name} is an educational study tool operated by {company.legalName}. It is not an
        official DMV product and does not guarantee that you will pass any DMV exam. Subscriptions
        are billed by Apple App Store or Google Play. These Terms are governed by the laws of{" "}
        {company.state}.
      </div>
    </header>

    <nav aria-label="Table of contents" class="mt-10 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-700 uppercase tracking-wide">Contents</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-indigo-700">
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#acceptance">1. Acceptance of These Terms</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#eligibility">2. Eligibility and Age Requirements</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#license">3. Educational License and Permitted Use</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#subscriptions">4. Subscriptions, Billing, and Renewal</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#refunds">5. Refunds and Cancellation</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#ip">6. Intellectual Property and Content Rights</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#conduct">7. Prohibited Conduct</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#disclaimer">8. Disclaimer of Warranties</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#liability">9. Limitation of Liability</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#governing">10. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#changes">11. Changes to the App or Terms</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#contact">12. Contact Information</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      <section id="acceptance">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">1. Acceptance of These Terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          By downloading, accessing, or using {product.name} (the "App"), you agree to these Terms
          of Service and to our Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, do not use the App.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          In these Terms, "{product.name}," "we," "us," and "our" refer to {company.legalName}, a
          limited liability company organized under the laws of the State of {company.state}{" "}
          (IL File Number {company.ilFileNumber}), the operator of the App. "You" refers to the
          person using the App.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="eligibility">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">2. Eligibility and Age Requirements</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The App is intended for people preparing for a DMV written exam. You should be at least
          16 years old to use the App independently. If you are under 16, you may use the App only
          with the involvement of a parent or legal guardian.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you are under 13, please use the App only with parental or guardian permission and
          supervision. The App is not designed as a service directed to children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="license">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">3. Educational License and Permitted Use</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Subject to these Terms, we grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
          revocable license to use the App for your personal, non-commercial study purposes.
        </p>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Educational Use Only</h3>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The App is provided for study and review only. It is not an official DMV product, does
          not provide legal advice, and does not guarantee that you will pass any DMV knowledge or
          written exam. Actual exam content, scoring, and legal requirements may change at any
          time.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-600">
          You remain responsible for checking the most current driver handbook, laws, and official
          DMV guidance for your state.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="subscriptions">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">4. Subscriptions, Billing, and Renewal</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Some features of the App may require a paid subscription. Available subscription plans
          may include weekly, monthly, and annual options shown in the App at the time of purchase.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>Subscriptions are billed through Apple App Store or Google Play, depending on your device.</li>
          <li>
            Subscriptions renew automatically unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the end of
            the current billing period, or as otherwise stated by your app marketplace.
          </li>
          <li>Prices, currencies, and tax treatment may vary by storefront, region, and applicable law.</li>
          <li>
            We use RevenueCat to validate subscription status and entitlements, but billing is
            processed by the platform store.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="refunds">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">5. Refunds and Cancellation</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Refunds and subscription cancellations are handled by the platform through which you
          made the purchase. We do not directly issue or manage store refunds.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>
            <strong>iOS:</strong> manage or cancel your subscription through your Apple Account
            subscription settings. Refund requests are handled by Apple under Apple policies.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Android:</strong> manage or cancel your subscription through Google Play.
            Refund requests are handled under Google Play policies.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you uninstall the App, your subscription does not automatically cancel. You must
          cancel through the applicable app marketplace.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="ip">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">6. Intellectual Property and Content Rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The App, including its study flows, text, explanations, translations, design, branding,
          and original images, is protected by intellectual property laws. State handbook concepts
          may be based on public government materials, but our organization, translations, practice
          items, and presentation remain protected.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You may not copy, sell, scrape, republish, or redistribute the App's content except as
          allowed by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="conduct">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">7. Prohibited Conduct</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>reverse engineer, decompile, tamper with, or attempt to extract source code from the App;</li>
          <li>circumvent subscription restrictions or misuse trial, purchase, or restore flows;</li>
          <li>copy, reproduce, or commercially redistribute App content without authorization;</li>
          <li>use the App in a way that interferes with its operation, security, or analytics integrity;</li>
          <li>use the App for unlawful, fraudulent, or abusive purposes.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="disclaimer">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">8. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The App is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis to the maximum extent
          permitted by law. We do not promise uninterrupted availability, error-free operation, or
          that the content will always match the latest DMV testing standards in every
          jurisdiction.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          To the extent permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, whether express, implied, or
          statutory, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
          purpose, and non-infringement.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="liability">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental,
          special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of data, revenue, profits,
          or exam outcomes arising from or related to your use of the App.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We are also not responsible for decisions made using the App's study content, including
          reliance on explanations, translations, or practice results. You are responsible for
          verifying current rules with official state sources.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="governing">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">10. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of {company.state}, without regard to
          its conflict-of-laws principles. Any dispute arising out of or relating to these Terms
          or your use of the App will be resolved exclusively in the state or federal courts
          located in Cook County, {company.state}, and you consent to the personal jurisdiction
          of those courts.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Nothing in this section limits any non-waivable rights you may have under the laws of
          your country of residence.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">11. Changes to the App or Terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may update the App, features, pricing, or these Terms from time to time. When we
          update these Terms, we will revise the version number and "Last updated" date on this
          page. Continued use of the App after updated Terms take effect means you accept the
          revised Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">12. Contact Information</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you have questions about these Terms, contact{" "}
          <a class="text-indigo-700 underline" href={`mailto:${product.emails.support}`}>
            {product.emails.support}
          </a>. For legal notices, write to{" "}
          <a class="text-indigo-700 underline" href={`mailto:${company.emails.legal}`}>
            {company.emails.legal}
          </a>{" "}
          or to our mailing address below.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 text-sm">
          <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Operator</p>
          <address class="not-italic mt-2 text-slate-700 leading-6">
            {company.legalName}<br />
            {company.address.line1}<br />
            {company.address.cityStateZip}<br />
            {company.address.country}
          </address>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
            Illinois Limited Liability Company · IL File Number {company.ilFileNumber}
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 text-sm text-slate-500">
      <p>
        {product.name} Terms of Service · Version {product.legalDocsVersion.terms}
      </p>
      <p>Last updated: {product.legalDocsVersion.lastUpdated}</p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
